In article <5254@ur-cc.UUCP>, ars3_cif@uhura.cc.rochester.edu (Aaron Sher) writes:
> Being polymorphed into a human has random effects on ability scores and
> level.

In a recent game, I got my wizard up to experience level 7, something
like 60 hps.  Got bitten by a werejackal, and my god wouldn't help me.
So I started using a ring of polymorph to change more quickly.
Polymorphing from a jackalwere, I always turned into a human with 4
hps.  That guy would get killed right away, then I would revert back
to my normal self.

Later in the game, with polymorph control (which kept me from becoming
a jackalwere), I turned into a new human.  Strength was about the
same, but hps were something like 11.  This with a exp level 11
character!  No matter how many time I changed into a new person, the
hps never went above 15.  Shouldn't the characters stats be more in
line with its experience level?

